HiRISE terrain crop (data)
--------------------------
public/terrain/hirise-lefroy-bay/ (the HiRISE model on the Mars Base map, built by
scripts/build-hirise-terrain.mjs) is a bounded crop of two NASA Solar System Treks (Mars Trek), JPL
products, recorded in src/data/sources.json:
  - MRO HiRISE, Jezero DEM, Controlled
    (JEZ_hirise_soc_006_DTM_MOLAtopography_DeltaGeoid_1m_Eqc_latTs0_lon0_blend40), id trek-jezero-hirise-dtm;
  - MRO HiRISE, Jezero Mosaic, Controlled
    (JEZ_hirise_soc_006_orthoMosaic_25cm_Eqc_latTs0_lon0_first_dd), id trek-jezero-hirise-ortho.
Their Mars Trek catalogue records (checked 2026-11-19):
  - give the mission and instrument as Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter / HiRISE;
  - state that the USGS Astrogeology Science Center generated and delivered the HiRISE DTM mosaic and
    orthomosaic, in support of the Mars 2020 Terrain Relative Navigation.
The existing map attribution "NASA/JPL/UArizona" is kept. It does not appear in these catalogue
records; that alone does not show that it is wrong. It is to be checked against the source of the
specific product.

